; ============================================================
;  EventProbe hook declaration (Syringe .inj)
;
;  MUST BE PURE ASCII -- Syringe parses this file as ANSI text.
;  No Chinese, no BOM, no smart quotes. Keep comments in English.
;
;  Format:   ADDRESS = FunctionName, BytesOverwritten
; ============================================================

; ---- Main sampling point ----
; Inside Execute_DoList, the instruction that reads DoList.Count:
;
;     64c38d:  8b 3d f8 41 8b 00    mov   0x8b41f8,%edi     (exactly 6 bytes)
;
;  Why not the function entry 0x64C380:
;    1) 0x64C380 needs a 10-byte overwrite which includes
;       `sub esp` and `push` (two stack-modifying instructions).
;       With it installed the game crashes every time -- except.txt shows a
;       trampoline reading 0xC35AE9F8 while the real instruction should read
;       0xA80238. Reproduced on both plain YR and Mental Omega.
;    2) 0x64C38D is a single instruction, absolute addressing, no stack use.
;    3) Same timing: DoList is already populated at this point.
;
;  Byte-identical on both gamemd builds we checked (4813072 / 4816864 bytes).
0x64C38D = EventProbe_ExecuteEventsHook, 6

; ---- Heartbeat / fallback sampling point ----
; Main loop per-logical-frame entry. Same address used by ChatBox / AutoKit /
; Phobos / AutoLoad, so it is well proven.
;
;  NOTE: measured -- DoList is still EMPTY at this moment; the current frame's
;  events are only inserted later during the frame. So this hook alone yields
;  no data. Its job is to prove the probe is alive ("hook: frame alive") and to
;  keep the probe usable (with an explicit "DoList empty" diagnostic) if the
;  main sampling point above ever has to be removed.
0x55D360 = EventProbe_FrameHook, 5
